From: zbai29 <zbai29@wisc.edu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add paseo send --system for external-wait resumes

Incremental on top of the finish-deferral companion patch. Vanilla checkouts
should apply external-wait-finish-deferral.patch instead (it already includes
this).

Rebased onto getpaseo/paseo v0.11.4 (dc5b02f7d) plus finish deferral.
PaseoAgentSendOptions is now an alias of SendMessageOptions, so the system
flag lives only on that interface.

---
diff --git a/docs/agent-lifecycle.md b/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
--- a/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
+++ b/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
@@ -96,6 +96,9 @@ The label marks an external controller's ownership; Paseo does not interpret the
 the external system, group membership, or completion strategy. The controller must serialize its
 state transitions and completion prompts. Errors and permission requests still notify the caller
 immediately. Clearing the label while the child is idle does not itself complete the delegated task.
+External controllers should resume the child with `paseo send --system`; this uses the same hidden
+system-context path as child-to-parent finish notifications instead of adding a user-message bubble
+to the timeline.
 Permission requests are notification checkpoints, not the end of that subscription. The caller is notified again after a permission response when the child finishes, errors, or requests another permission.
 The permission notification includes the normalized request plus the child and request IDs, so the caller can inspect it and respond without fetching agent status.
 A watched child that closes before its finish event also notifies the caller so delegated work cannot disappear silently during archive or workspace teardown.
